<div class="acp-page-container">
	<div component="settings/main/header" class="row border-bottom pb-3 mb-4 align-items-center">
		<div class="col-sm-12">
			<h2 class="m-0 fw-semibold tracking-tight">BlockNote Composer</h2>
		</div>
	</div>

	<div class="row">
		<div class="col-sm-12">
			<div class="card">
				<div class="card-body">
					<h3>About BlockNote Composer</h3>
					<p>
						The BlockNote Composer provides a modern, user-friendly WYSIWYG editing experience for your forum users.
					</p>

					<h4>Features</h4>
					<ul>
						<li>True WYSIWYG editing (What You See Is What You Get)</li>
						<li>Rich text formatting (bold, italic, underline, strikethrough, code)</li>
						<li>Image uploads with drag & drop</li>
						<li>File attachments</li>
						<li>Link formatting</li>
						<li>Multiple block types (headings, lists, code blocks, tables)</li>
						<li>Slash commands for quick block insertion</li>
						<li>Mobile-friendly interface</li>
					</ul>

					<h4>Requirements</h4>
					<p class="alert alert-warning">
						<strong>Important:</strong> To use BlockNote Composer, you must disable the default composer plugin (<code>nodebb-plugin-composer-default</code>) in the Plugins section.
					</p>

					<h4>Usage</h4>
					<p>
						Once enabled, users will automatically see the BlockNote editor when creating new topics or replies.
						They can use slash commands (type <code>/</code>) to quickly insert different block types.
					</p>

					<h4>Support</h4>
					<p>
						For issues or feature requests, visit:
						<a href="https://github.com/sarah-tbrpc/nodebb-plugin-composer-blocknote/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
							GitHub Issues
						</a>
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</div>
